Yes — and the first thing to separate is:
	•	true breaks = is_terminal = true
	•	not expanded yet = is_terminal = false

If your run stopped because of a guard, some paths did not break; they just were not expanded yet.

Use this query pack.

1) Did lineage actually break, or did the run just stop first?

SELECT
  is_terminal,
  COUNT(*) AS path_rows,
  COUNT(DISTINCT leaf_table) AS distinct_leaf_tables,
  MIN(hop_count) AS min_hop,
  MAX(hop_count) AS max_hop
FROM cdo.npd_current_pending_upstream_paths_current_7d_v
GROUP BY is_terminal
ORDER BY is_terminal DESC;

How to read it:
	•	is_terminal = true → true lineage breaks/endpoints in the 7-day graph
	•	is_terminal = false → still-active paths that were left unfinished because the run stopped

2) Where do true breaks happen by hop?

SELECT
  hop_count AS break_hop,
  COUNT(*) AS terminal_path_rows,
  COUNT(DISTINCT leaf_table) AS terminal_leaf_tables
FROM cdo.npd_current_pending_upstream_paths_current_7d_v
WHERE is_terminal = true
GROUP BY hop_count
ORDER BY break_hop;

This shows which hop levels have the most breaks.

3) What are the most common broken leaf tables?

SELECT
  hop_count AS break_hop,
  leaf_table,
  COUNT(*) AS terminal_path_rows,
  MAX(
    CASE
      WHEN size(edge_latest_seen_times) = 0 THEN CAST(NULL AS TIMESTAMP)
      ELSE array_max(edge_latest_seen_times)
    END
  ) AS latest_seen_time_on_path
FROM cdo.npd_current_pending_upstream_paths_current_7d_v
WHERE is_terminal = true
GROUP BY
  hop_count,
  leaf_table
ORDER BY
  terminal_path_rows DESC,
  break_hop,
  leaf_table
LIMIT 200;

This tells you which leaf tables are most often the endpoint of a broken path.

4) Why did each path break?

This is the main diagnostic query.

WITH terminal_paths AS (
  SELECT
    path_id,
    hop_count AS break_hop,
    leaf_table,
    path_tables,
    window_start,
    window_end
  FROM cdo.npd_current_pending_upstream_paths_current_7d_v
  WHERE is_terminal = true
),
parents_7d AS (
  SELECT
    t.path_id,
    COUNT(DISTINCT e.source_table_full_name) AS parents_in_7d
  FROM terminal_paths t
  LEFT JOIN cdo.npd_current_pending_lineage_edges_7d e
    ON t.leaf_table = e.target_table_full_name
   AND e.source_table_full_name <> e.target_table_full_name
  GROUP BY t.path_id
),
eligible_new_parents_7d AS (
  SELECT
    t.path_id,
    COUNT(DISTINCT e.source_table_full_name) AS eligible_new_parents_in_7d
  FROM terminal_paths t
  LEFT JOIN cdo.npd_current_pending_lineage_edges_7d e
    ON t.leaf_table = e.target_table_full_name
   AND e.source_table_full_name <> e.target_table_full_name
   AND NOT array_contains(t.path_tables, e.source_table_full_name)
  GROUP BY t.path_id
),
parents_before_window AS (
  SELECT
    t.path_id,
    COUNT(DISTINCT l.source_table_full_name) AS parents_before_window
  FROM terminal_paths t
  LEFT JOIN information_schema.table_lineage l
    ON t.leaf_table = l.target_table_full_name
   AND l.source_table_full_name IS NOT NULL
   AND l.target_table_full_name IS NOT NULL
   AND l.source_table_full_name <> l.target_table_full_name
   AND l.event_time < t.window_start
  GROUP BY t.path_id
),
self_links_7d AS (
  SELECT
    t.path_id,
    COUNT(*) AS self_links_7d
  FROM terminal_paths t
  LEFT JOIN cdo.npd_current_pending_lineage_edges_7d e
    ON t.leaf_table = e.target_table_full_name
   AND e.source_table_full_name = e.target_table_full_name
  GROUP BY t.path_id
),
write_only_7d AS (
  SELECT
    t.path_id,
    COUNT(DISTINCT l.event_id) AS write_only_events_7d
  FROM terminal_paths t
  LEFT JOIN information_schema.table_lineage l
    ON t.leaf_table = l.target_table_full_name
   AND l.source_table_full_name IS NULL
   AND l.target_table_full_name IS NOT NULL
   AND l.event_time >= t.window_start
   AND l.event_time <= t.window_end
  GROUP BY t.path_id
)
SELECT
  t.break_hop,
  t.leaf_table,
  COALESCE(p.parents_in_7d, 0) AS parents_in_7d,
  COALESCE(enp.eligible_new_parents_in_7d, 0) AS eligible_new_parents_in_7d,
  COALESCE(pbw.parents_before_window, 0) AS parents_before_window,
  COALESCE(sl.self_links_7d, 0) AS self_links_7d,
  COALESCE(wo.write_only_events_7d, 0) AS write_only_events_7d,
  CASE
    WHEN COALESCE(enp.eligible_new_parents_in_7d, 0) > 0 THEN 'SHOULD_HAVE_EXPANDED_CHECK_LOGIC'
    WHEN COALESCE(p.parents_in_7d, 0) > 0
         AND COALESCE(enp.eligible_new_parents_in_7d, 0) = 0 THEN 'CYCLE_OR_ALREADY_VISITED'
    WHEN COALESCE(sl.self_links_7d, 0) > 0
         AND COALESCE(p.parents_in_7d, 0) = 0 THEN 'SELF_LINK_ONLY'
    WHEN COALESCE(pbw.parents_before_window, 0) > 0 THEN 'UPSTREAM_OUTSIDE_7D_WINDOW'
    WHEN COALESCE(wo.write_only_events_7d, 0) > 0 THEN 'WRITE_ONLY_OR_UNINFERRED_IN_7D'
    ELSE 'NO_VISIBLE_UPSTREAM'
  END AS break_reason,
  t.path_id,
  t.path_tables
FROM terminal_paths t
LEFT JOIN parents_7d p
  ON t.path_id = p.path_id
LEFT JOIN eligible_new_parents_7d enp
  ON t.path_id = enp.path_id
LEFT JOIN parents_before_window pbw
  ON t.path_id = pbw.path_id
LEFT JOIN self_links_7d sl
  ON t.path_id = sl.path_id
LEFT JOIN write_only_7d wo
  ON t.path_id = wo.path_id
ORDER BY
  t.break_hop DESC,
  break_reason,
  t.leaf_table;

How to read the break_reason values:
	•	CYCLE_OR_ALREADY_VISITED → upstream exists in 7 days, but only through objects already on the path
	•	SELF_LINK_ONLY → only self-links were found, and we exclude those from traversal
	•	UPSTREAM_OUTSIDE_7D_WINDOW → lineage exists, but only before the 7-day cutoff
	•	WRITE_ONLY_OR_UNINFERRED_IN_7D → target had write activity, but no usable source->target edge in the 7-day window
	•	NO_VISIBLE_UPSTREAM → nothing visible in lineage for that leaf
	•	SHOULD_HAVE_EXPANDED_CHECK_LOGIC → this should usually be zero; if not, there is probably a logic bug in the traversal

5) Summarize break reasons

WITH terminal_diagnostics AS (
  WITH terminal_paths AS (
    SELECT
      path_id,
      hop_count AS break_hop,
      leaf_table,
      path_tables,
      window_start,
      window_end
    FROM cdo.npd_current_pending_upstream_paths_current_7d_v
    WHERE is_terminal = true
  ),
  parents_7d AS (
    SELECT
      t.path_id,
      COUNT(DISTINCT e.source_table_full_name) AS parents_in_7d
    FROM terminal_paths t
    LEFT JOIN cdo.npd_current_pending_lineage_edges_7d e
      ON t.leaf_table = e.target_table_full_name
     AND e.source_table_full_name <> e.target_table_full_name
    GROUP BY t.path_id
  ),
  eligible_new_parents_7d AS (
    SELECT
      t.path_id,
      COUNT(DISTINCT e.source_table_full_name) AS eligible_new_parents_in_7d
    FROM terminal_paths t
    LEFT JOIN cdo.npd_current_pending_lineage_edges_7d e
      ON t.leaf_table = e.target_table_full_name
     AND e.source_table_full_name <> e.target_table_full_name
     AND NOT array_contains(t.path_tables, e.source_table_full_name)
    GROUP BY t.path_id
  ),
  parents_before_window AS (
    SELECT
      t.path_id,
      COUNT(DISTINCT l.source_table_full_name) AS parents_before_window
    FROM terminal_paths t
    LEFT JOIN information_schema.table_lineage l
      ON t.leaf_table = l.target_table_full_name
     AND l.source_table_full_name IS NOT NULL
     AND l.target_table_full_name IS NOT NULL
     AND l.source_table_full_name <> l.target_table_full_name
     AND l.event_time < t.window_start
    GROUP BY t.path_id
  ),
  self_links_7d AS (
    SELECT
      t.path_id,
      COUNT(*) AS self_links_7d
    FROM terminal_paths t
    LEFT JOIN cdo.npd_current_pending_lineage_edges_7d e
      ON t.leaf_table = e.target_table_full_name
     AND e.source_table_full_name = e.target_table_full_name
    GROUP BY t.path_id
  ),
  write_only_7d AS (
    SELECT
      t.path_id,
      COUNT(DISTINCT l.event_id) AS write_only_events_7d
    FROM terminal_paths t
    LEFT JOIN information_schema.table_lineage l
      ON t.leaf_table = l.target_table_full_name
     AND l.source_table_full_name IS NULL
     AND l.target_table_full_name IS NOT NULL
     AND l.event_time >= t.window_start
     AND l.event_time <= t.window_end
    GROUP BY t.path_id
  )
  SELECT
    t.break_hop,
    CASE
      WHEN COALESCE(enp.eligible_new_parents_in_7d, 0) > 0 THEN 'SHOULD_HAVE_EXPANDED_CHECK_LOGIC'
      WHEN COALESCE(p.parents_in_7d, 0) > 0
           AND COALESCE(enp.eligible_new_parents_in_7d, 0) = 0 THEN 'CYCLE_OR_ALREADY_VISITED'
      WHEN COALESCE(sl.self_links_7d, 0) > 0
           AND COALESCE(p.parents_in_7d, 0) = 0 THEN 'SELF_LINK_ONLY'
      WHEN COALESCE(pbw.parents_before_window, 0) > 0 THEN 'UPSTREAM_OUTSIDE_7D_WINDOW'
      WHEN COALESCE(wo.write_only_events_7d, 0) > 0 THEN 'WRITE_ONLY_OR_UNINFERRED_IN_7D'
      ELSE 'NO_VISIBLE_UPSTREAM'
    END AS break_reason
  FROM terminal_paths t
  LEFT JOIN parents_7d p
    ON t.path_id = p.path_id
  LEFT JOIN eligible_new_parents_7d enp
    ON t.path_id = enp.path_id
  LEFT JOIN parents_before_window pbw
    ON t.path_id = pbw.path_id
  LEFT JOIN self_links_7d sl
    ON t.path_id = sl.path_id
  LEFT JOIN write_only_7d wo
    ON t.path_id = wo.path_id
)
SELECT
  break_hop,
  break_reason,
  COUNT(*) AS terminal_paths
FROM terminal_diagnostics
GROUP BY
  break_hop,
  break_reason
ORDER BY
  break_hop,
  terminal_paths DESC,
  break_reason;

6) Show unfinished paths too

This is useful when a safety guard stopped the run.

SELECT
  hop_count,
  leaf_table,
  path_id,
  path_tables
FROM cdo.npd_current_pending_upstream_paths_current_7d_v
WHERE is_terminal = false
ORDER BY hop_count DESC, leaf_table;

If you want, I can also give you one query that highlights only the most suspicious breaks — for example:
	•	SHOULD_HAVE_EXPANDED_CHECK_LOGIC
	•	UPSTREAM_OUTSIDE_7D_WINDOW
	•	WRITE_ONLY_OR_UNINFERRED_IN_7D
